# One-shot job image that upgrades a PostgreSQL 17 data directory to 18 in place.
#
# Railway's dashboard upgrade (Database > Config > Major Version Upgrade) only runs for
# services on Railway's own postgres-ssl image, so it is unavailable to services on
# ghcr.io/fountain-bio/postgres. This image runs the same upgrade job that flow uses:
# Railway's published 17-to-18 job image, which carries both majors' server binaries and
# runs `pg_upgrade --link` through upgrade-job.sh against the service's own volume.
#
# pg_cron has to be added for both majors. Our volumes preload pg_cron, so the 17 server
# cannot start without postgresql-17-cron, and pg_upgrade's loadable-libraries check fails
# unless postgresql-18-cron is present for the new cluster. upgrade-job.sh copies the old
# cluster's shared_preload_libraries onto the 18 server when the .so exists, and pg_cron
# skips starting its scheduler while pg_upgrade runs the servers in binary-upgrade mode.
#
# Runbook, per database service. The job runs as a deployment of the database service so it
# gets the service's volume and variables (PGDATA, POSTGRES_USER):
#   1. Take a backup of the service.
#   2. Set the service's restart policy to Never so a failed job is not rerun on its own.
#      Set the service variable UPGRADE_JOB_MODE=check, set Source Image to
#      ghcr.io/fountain-bio/postgres:upgrade-17-18, and deploy. The database is down from here
#      until step 5. The job exits after one run; read the RAILWAY_UPGRADE_RESULT line in the
#      deploy logs. Exit 1 lists blockers to fix on 17 before continuing.
#   3. Set UPGRADE_JOB_MODE=upgrade and redeploy. The job writes a completion marker on the
#      volume once pg_upgrade succeeds, then swaps directories. Re-running upgrade mode after
#      a crash resumes from the marker.
#   4. Remove UPGRADE_JOB_MODE and put the restart policy back.
#   5. Set Source Image to ghcr.io/fountain-bio/postgres:18 and deploy. The 18 image's
#      wrapper refuses to boot while an unfinished marker exists or the data directory is
#      on another major.
# To back out before step 3 commits, deploy with UPGRADE_JOB_MODE=recover, then return the
# Source Image to ghcr.io/fountain-bio/postgres:17. After the commit point, restore the backup.
#
# The job requires the volume mounted at /var/lib/postgresql/data with PGDATA beneath it,
# which is the layout Railway's 17 template created.
#
# The base is pinned by digest because Railway publishes this image only under the moving
# `17-18` tag.
FROM ghcr.io/railwayapp-templates/postgres-ssl/upgrade:17-18@sha256:b6ff5fcb8a45da6f132fa60c8369d33a562b28d5a0d7ef3a52404b8bf575531f

# The base image's PGDG apt source already lists both the 17 and 18 components. Holding the
# server packages keeps this install from moving either bundled minor.
RUN apt-mark hold postgresql-17 postgresql-client-17 postgresql-18 postgresql-client-18 \
  && apt-get update \
  && apt-get install -y --no-install-recommends postgresql-17-cron postgresql-18-cron \
  && apt-mark unhold postgresql-17 postgresql-client-17 postgresql-18 postgresql-client-18 \
  && rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/*
